                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
                in terms of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                over
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+categories"} comma categories
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Functors"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \;\colon\; \mathcal{D} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorsInTermsOfNaturalBijectionOfHomSets"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
                  all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Limits"}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒟
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathcal{D}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Limits"}
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CanonicalFunctorOutOfCommaCategoryOfcOverF"} (?)
                  out of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                  (Example
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CommaCategoryWithOneSideConstant"}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi R
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d/R \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
                %p exists.
            %p
              In this case the value of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              is given by that limit:
            #eq:FormulaForLeftAdjointByPointwiseLimit.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (9)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mrow
                              %mtable
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi d
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %msup
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                      %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                        %mi f
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi R
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi c
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi R
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(d)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\underset{\underset{ \left( c,  \array{ d \\ \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} \\ R(c) } \right)  \in d/R }{\longleftarrow}}{\lim} c
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p First assume that the left adjoint exist. Then
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  and hence preserves limits since all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoints+preserve+limits"} right adjoints preserve limits
                  (Prop.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointsPreserveCoLimits"}
              %li
                %p
                  by Prop.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CollectionOfUniversalArrowsEquivalentToAdjointFunctor"}
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
                  provides a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+morphism"} universal morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_d
                  into
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(d)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalMorphismsAreInitialObjectsInCommaCategory"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L(d), \eta_d)
                  as the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d/R
            %p
              Conversely, assume that the two conditions are satisfied and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(d)
              be given by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FormulaForLeftAdjointByPointwiseLimit"} (9)
            %p
              By the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              preserves all limits that exist, we have
            #eq:RAppliedtoFormulaForLeftAdjointByPointwiseLimit.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (10)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi R
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mi lim
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟵
                                  %mrow
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo (
                                      %mi c
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mrow
                                        %mtable
                                          %mtr
                                            %mtd
                                              %mi d
                                          %mtr
                                            %mtd
                                              %msup
                                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                                  %mi f
                                          %mtr
                                            %mtd
                                              %mi R
                                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                              %mi c
                                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                      %mo )
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi d
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                    %mi R
                              %mi c
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo (
                                    %mi c
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mrow
                                      %mtable
                                        %mtr
                                          %mtd
                                            %mi d
                                        %mtr
                                          %mtd
                                            %msup
                                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                                %mi f
                                        %mtr
                                          %mtd
                                            %mi R
                                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                            %mi c
                                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo )
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi d
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                  %mi R
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    R(L(d))
                    \&amp; =
                    R\left(
                    \\underset{\underset{ \left( c,  \array{ d \\ \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} \\ R(c) } \right)  \in d/R }{\longleftarrow}}{\lim} c
                    \\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\underset{\underset{ \left( c,  \array{ d \\ \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} \\ R(c) } \right)  \in d/R }{\longleftarrow}}{\lim} R(c)
                    }
            %p
              Since the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \overset{f}{\to} R(d)
              constitute a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(d)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi d
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d \overset{\phantom{AA} \eta_d \phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow} R(L(d))
                    \\,.
            %p
              By Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CollectionOfUniversalArrowsEquivalentToAdjointFunctor"}
              it is now sufficient to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_d
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+morphism"} universal morphism
              into
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(d)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi g
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \overset{g}{\longrightarrow} R(c)
              there is a unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ˜
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(d) \overset{\widetilde f}{\longrightarrow} c
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi d
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %mi R
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ˜
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ˜
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; d
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{ \eta_d }}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    R(L(d)) &amp;&amp; \underset{\phantom{AA}R(\widetilde f)\phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; R(c)
                    \\\
                    L(d)
                    \&amp;&amp;\underset{\phantom{AA}\widetilde f\phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;&amp;
                    c
                    }
            %p
              By Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalMorphismsAreInitialObjectsInCommaCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L(d), \eta_d)
              being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c/R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c/R
              (by Example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InitialObjectIsLimitOverIdentityFunctor"}
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FormulaForLeftAdjointByPointwiseLimit"} (9)
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RAppliedtoFormulaForLeftAdjointByPointwiseLimit"} (10)
          #AdjointFunctorTheorem.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"}> adjoint functor theorem
                )
            %p
              Beware the subtle point in Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointwiseExpressionOfLeftAdjoints"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c/F
              is in general not a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              (Def.
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmallCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              has, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is not assumed to be small (while of course it may happen to be). But typical categories, such as notably the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
              (Example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfSets"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointwiseExpressionOfLeftAdjoints"}
              is rarely useful for
              %em finding
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              which is not already established to exist by other means.
            %p
              But there are good sufficient conditions known, on top of the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              preserves limits, which guarantee the existence of an adjoint functor, after all. This is the topic of the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
              (one of the rare instances of useful and non-trivial theorems in mathematics for which issues of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theoretic
              size play a crucial role for their statement and proof).
            %p
              A very special but also very useful case of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
              is the existence of adjoints of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              functors between categories of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+presheaf"}> enriched
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
              via
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalLeftKanExtensionBCoend"}
              below. Since this is most conveniently phrased in terms of special
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              called
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ends"} ends
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EndAndCoendInTopcgSmash"}
              below) we first discuss these.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#TopologicalEndsAndCoends Ends and coends
          %p
            For working with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopEnrichedCategory"}
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Limits"}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ends"} ends
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EndAndCoendInTopcgSmash"}
            below). We here introduce these and then derive some of their basic properties, such as notably the expression for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            in terms of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"}> co-
